ate\nthis morning and continue falling to 3.9 feet Tuesday morning.\n- Flood stage is 25.0 feet.\n- Flood History...This crest compares to a previous crest of 25.8\nfeet on 06/13/1981.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","instruction":"Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nMotorists should not attempt to drive around barricades or drive cars\nthrough flooded areas.\n\nCaution is urged when walking near riverbanks.\n\nEven 6 inches of fast-moving flood water can knock you off your feet\nand a depth of 2 feet will float your car. Never try to walk, swim,\nor drive through such swift water. If you come upon flood waters,\nstop, turn around and go another way.\n\nAdditional information is available at www.weather.gov/crp.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["FLSCRP"],"WMOidentifier":["WGUS84 KCRP 061331"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.EXT.KCRP.FL.W.0027.000000T0000Z-260807T0738Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-08-07T02:38:00-05:00"],"expiredReferences":["w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.15a54361c4ea7596611f53154fbe235d68afe15a.001.1,2026-08-05T10:56:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.cfe0cb53516243e5682c1b93f097af5f347ba9d1.001.1,2026-08-04T20:07:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.0d85f3f3b48cc9017f55a16e1f1acf4cc74e9f0b.001.1,2026-08-04T15:51:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.52c53adf21b8a3c6773f1bc49de7351006f6e777.001.1,2026-08-04T08:54:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1890e16dec93bc7bd2c40c556f7d88b51dfba240.001.1,2026-08-03T20:13:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6c2d46f696ba508a8268a87165a57be61f4e50bb.001.1,2026-08-03T09:17:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a89341f8395f18ac2219ce1a412989c19cd5d270.001.1,2026-08-02T20:24:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.135a0f1988967